## 2. Motivation

The motivation behind Plant Pal stems from several real-world observations:

- **Growing interest in indoor gardening:** Urban residents, including students and office workers, increasingly keep potted plants but often lack the expertise to maintain them properly. Plants frequently die from neglect or improper care.
- **Gap in existing solutions:** Commercial plant monitors exist but typically provide only raw sensor readings without intelligent analysis or actionable advice. Users still need to interpret the data themselves.
- **Convergence of IoT and AI:** The rapid development of IoT sensor technology and large language models (LLMs) creates a unique opportunity to build systems that not only sense but also *understand* and *communicate* plant needs.
- **Voice as a natural interface:** Traditional plant monitoring systems require users to check apps or dashboards. Voice interaction removes this friction — users can simply ask "How is my plant doing?" and receive an intelligent response.
- **Practical learning opportunity:** This project provides hands-on experience with end-to-end IoT system design, from hardware sensor integration and firmware development to cloud-based AI agents and voice-enabled user interfaces, covering the full spectrum of IoT technologies taught in EIE568.

---

## 3. Achievable Objectives

- **Integrate multiple environmental sensors** — DHT11 (temperature and humidity), HW-390 (soil moisture), and a light sensor — onto an Arduino-based sensor node for comprehensive plant environment monitoring.
- **Implement MQTT-based data telemetry** — Publish sensor readings to an MQTT broker every 30 minutes, enabling reliable and lightweight data transmission from the sensor node to the cloud.
- **Deploy a cloud-based AI analysis agent (OpenClaw)** — Subscribe to sensor data, maintain a plant care knowledge base, and generate automated plant health assessments.
- **Establish scheduled reporting via Feishu** — Automatically push plant status summaries and care recommendations to a Feishu channel every 6 hours using cron-based scheduling.
- **Enable voice interaction through xiaozhi ESP32** — Allow users to query plant status, receive care suggestions, and analyze plant conditions through camera imagery via natural language voice commands.
- **Implement cross-agent communication** — Establish bidirectional data flow between the xiaozhi voice agent and the OpenClaw cloud agent using webhook, WebSocket, and MCP (Model Context Protocol) for seamless integration.
- **Deliver a complete, demonstrable end-to-end prototype** — Showcase the full pipeline from sensor data collection through AI analysis to user-facing voice interaction and push notifications.

