## 9. Results, Conclusion & Scope of Future Work

### Results

The Plant Pal system successfully demonstrated end-to-end functionality across all three core pillars:

**Sensor Data Collection:**
The Arduino sensor node reliably collects environmental data every 30 minutes. A sample reading:

| Parameter | Value | Timestamp |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| 🌡️ Temperature | 23.4°C | 2026-04-07 21:13:10 |
| 💧 Humidity | 70% | 2026-04-07 21:13:10 |
| 🌱 Soil Moisture | 44.1% | 2026-04-07 21:13:10 |
| 🌤️ Light | 74.41% | 2026-04-07 21:13:10 |

**Automated Cloud Analysis & Reporting:**
OpenClaw successfully analyzes sensor trends on a 6-hour schedule and pushes structured plant health reports to Feishu, including care recommendations based on current and historical data.

**Voice Interaction:**
Users can interact with the system through natural language via xiaozhi ESP32. Supported queries include:
- "What is the latest plant status data?"
- "What suggestions do you have regarding the plant's status?"
- "Can you take a picture and analyze the current status of the plant?"

The system responds with spoken advice that combines real-time sensor data with the AI agent's plant care knowledge.

### Conclusion

Plant Pal has successfully implemented three core functions — **Arduino sensor data collection**, **OpenClaw AI scheduled analysis with Feishu push notifications**, and **xiaozhi ESP32 voice interaction** — validating the feasibility of an integrated solution that combines IoT sensing, cloud AI, and voice interaction.

The project demonstrates that:
- MQTT is an effective lightweight protocol for IoT sensor data transmission in plant monitoring scenarios.
- Cloud-based AI agents can provide meaningful plant health assessments by combining sensor data with domain-specific knowledge.
- Voice interfaces significantly lower the barrier to entry for interacting with IoT systems, making plant care guidance accessible and intuitive.
- A modular architecture with standardized data formats (JSON) enables successful integration across heterogeneous platforms (C++ firmware, cloud agents, voice devices).

